* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.spv binary
*.bin binary
*.ttf binary

# Project documentation (the root README, docs/ and the builder guide) names release versions
# and download links, so source archives leave it out: GitHub's generated ZIP/TAR and the
# package_star_ocean.py source export both read these rules, and the docs can change after a
# release is built. Credits, license texts and third-party notices stay in every archive. The
# licenses folder itself is unset too: an ignored directory hides everything below it.
/README.md export-ignore
/packaging/linux/README.md export-ignore
/docs/** export-ignore
/docs/UPSTREAM_CREDITS.md -export-ignore
/docs/licenses -export-ignore
/docs/licenses/** -export-ignore
